---
import PolicyLayout from '../../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
---
<PolicyLayout
  appName="Beloti"
  icon="♠️"
  heading="Terms of Service"
  title="Beloti — Terms of Service"
  description="Effective date: August 30, 2026"
>
  <div class="card summary-card" slot="meta">
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Beloti is free and there is nothing to buy.</strong> No purchases, no subscriptions, no way to spend real money in the app at all.</li>
      <li><strong>Coins are not money.</strong> They have no monetary value, cannot be bought, sold or transferred, and cannot be exchanged for anything outside the game.</li>
      <li>You need to be <strong>16 or over</strong> to use Beloti.</li>
      <li>Play fairly: no automation, no exploiting bugs, and nothing that spoils a game for the other three people at the table.</li>
      <li>We can suspend an account that breaks these rules, and <strong>you can delete yours at any time from the app</strong>.</li>
      <li>These terms are governed by the law of Georgia. If you live in the EU or UK, your own country's consumer protections still apply to you.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>1. Who these terms are between</h2>
  <p>
    Beloti ("the app", "the game") is made and operated by <strong>Avtandigital</strong> ("we",
    "us", "our"). These terms are an agreement between you and us, and they apply whenever you
    use the app. If you do not accept them, do not use it — installing it, signing in and
    playing are all ways of accepting them.
  </p>
  <p>
    How we handle your information is a separate document and part of the same agreement: the
    <a href="/Beloti/privacy-policy.html">privacy policy</a>. Where the two overlap — account
    deletion, for instance — the privacy policy is the more detailed one.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Who can use Beloti</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>You must be at least 16 years old.</strong> The app is not intended for anyone
    younger and we do not knowingly let under-16s create an account. If you are under 16 and
    have created one, or you are a parent who believes your child has, contact us at the
    address in Section 12 and we will delete it.
  </p>
  <p>
    You also need to be able to enter into an agreement where you live, and you must not be
    barred from using the app by any law that applies to you.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Your account</h2>
  <p>
    You can play as a guest without giving us anything, or sign in with Apple or Google so your
    account survives changing phone. Either way it is a real account and it holds your coins and
    your match history.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>A guest account lives only on the device that created it.</strong> There is no way for us to recover one — no email, no password, nothing to identify it by. If you uninstall the app or lose the device, that account is gone, and so are its coins. Sign in with Apple or Google before you switch phones.</li>
    <li>Keep your Apple or Google account secure. Anyone who can sign in as you can play as you.</li>
    <li>One person, one account. Creating extra accounts to work around a suspension, or to funnel coins between them, is not allowed.</li>
    <li>You can delete your account from inside the app at any time. It is immediate and cannot be undone.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Coins</h2>
  <p>
    Coins are how a seat at a table is paid for. <strong>They are not money and never become
    money.</strong> Specifically:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>They have <strong>no monetary value</strong>, and no cash value at any time.</li>
    <li><strong>They cannot be bought.</strong> There are no purchases anywhere in the app.</li>
    <li>They cannot be sold, traded, gifted or transferred to another player.</li>
    <li>They cannot be exchanged for money, goods, or anything else outside the game.</li>
    <li>You do not own them. They are a feature of the game, not property, and they exist only inside your account.</li>
    <li>They are <strong>consumed when you sit down</strong> to a match, including when you ask for another match after one finishes. A rematch costs the same as any other match.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The amounts — what a match costs, what an ad is worth — are shown in the app and can change.
    We will not change them retroactively to take coins you have already earned.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>If we end a match ourselves, your entry fee comes back.</strong> That happens when
    the server restarts during a game, and the app tells you what was returned rather than
    asking you to take it on trust. If a match ends because you left it, it does not.
  </p>
  <p>
    We can correct a coin balance that is wrong — because of a bug, a failed payment of a
    reward, or coins obtained by breaking these terms. We will not take coins you earned
    legitimately.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Ads</h2>
  <p>
    Beloti is free and funded by optional rewarded ads. Watching one is always your choice: no
    ad ever interrupts a hand, and if you cannot afford a match the game gives you enough to
    keep playing, so you are never stuck behind an ad. Ads are served by Google AdMob — what
    that involves is described in Section 6 of the
    <a href="/Beloti/privacy-policy.html">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Trying to obtain rewards without genuinely watching an ad — automation, tampering with the
    app, or interfering with how rewards are confirmed — is a breach of these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Playing fairly</h2>
  <p>
    Three other people are in every match, and most of what follows is really one rule: do not
    spoil the game for them.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Do not use bots, scripts, modified clients or anything else that plays for you or tells you what to play.</li>
    <li>Do not exploit a bug. If you find one, tell us — see Section 12.</li>
    <li>Do not arrange results between accounts, or play to lose in order to move coins around.</li>
    <li>Do not deliberately stall. The game shortens the clock for seats that use all of it, and repeatedly abandoning matches is recorded.</li>
    <li>Do not interfere with the service, try to gain access to parts of it that are not yours, or attempt to work out other players' cards by any means other than playing the game.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="muted">
    Some seats at a table are played by the game itself. That is always disclosed in the app —
    a bot is labelled as one, including when a bot takes over a seat whose player has
    disconnected.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Your display name, and what you can say</h2>
  <p>
    Your display name is shown to the other three people at your table, so it has to be
    something they can reasonably be shown. Names that impersonate somebody, that are offensive,
    or that pretend to be part of the game itself are refused, and we can change or remove one
    that gets through. Names can be changed once a day.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>There is no chat in Beloti</strong>, and this is deliberate rather than unfinished:
    at a partnership card game, free text between partners is a way of passing information about
    a hand. The only things you can say at a table are a fixed set of emoji.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can report another player from the table. Reports are read by a person, and we act on
    them at our discretion.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Suspension and ending your access</h2>
  <p>
    We can suspend or close an account that breaks these terms. Where it is reasonable to do so
    we will say why, and a suspension can be temporary or permanent depending on what happened.
    Coins in a closed account are not refunded or transferred, because they were never money.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can stop using Beloti whenever you like, and delete your account from inside the app.
    Deleting removes your personal information immediately; what survives, and for how long, is
    set out in the privacy policy.
  </p>

  <h2>9. The service itself</h2>
  <p>
    Beloti is an online game, so it needs our server to work. We do not promise it will always
    be available, or free of bugs. <strong>Matches can be interrupted</strong> — most often
    because the server is being updated — and when that happens the entry fee goes back.
  </p>
  <p>
    We may change how the game works, add or remove features, or adjust the rules and the coin
    amounts. Where a change is significant we will make it visible in the app rather than
    quietly. We may also stop offering Beloti altogether; if we do, we will give what notice we
    reasonably can.
  </p>
  <p>
    The app is provided as it is. To the extent the law where you live allows it, we do not give
    warranties about it, and we are not liable for indirect or unforeseeable losses, or for lost
    coins, lost match history or lost progress. <strong>Nothing in these terms limits liability
    that cannot legally be limited</strong> — including for death or personal injury caused by
    negligence, or for fraud.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms — for instance if the game gains a feature these do not cover. The
    effective date above changes when we do, and continuing to use the app after that means you
    accept the revised terms. If a change materially reduces your rights, we will make it
    visible in the app rather than only here.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the law of <strong>Georgia</strong>, and the courts of Georgia
    have jurisdiction over any dispute arising from them.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>If you are a consumer in the European Union or the United Kingdom, this does not
    take away the protections of your own country's law.</strong> You keep the mandatory
    consumer rights you have where you live, and you can bring proceedings there. Our server is
    in Germany, which is described in the privacy policy.
  </p>
  <p>
    If any part of these terms turns out to be unenforceable, the rest still applies.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms, bug reports, or anything else about the app can be sent to
    <a href="mailto:avtukalaz@gmail.com">avtukalaz@gmail.com</a>.
  </p>

  <p class="muted" style="margin-top: 48px; padding-top: 20px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 0.85rem;">
    Beloti is a free online card game with no purchases of any kind; its coins are a game
    feature with no monetary value, as described in Section 4. These terms describe how the app
    actually works as implemented; they are provided as a starting point and have not been
    reviewed by a lawyer — consider a legal review before publishing to an app store, especially
    given the virtual currency and the EU consumers reached by a server in Germany.
  </p>
</PolicyLayout>
